WEBVTT

00:07.841 --> 00:10.759
Now, the thing about this one night,
and you guys know me.

00:10.760 --> 00:13.262
Like, I'm fuckin' easy on voters, right?

00:13.263 --> 00:15.347
- That ain't what they say.
- Oh, yeah, well, fuck them

00:15.348 --> 00:17.391
because they'd rather have me
than Greenberg.

00:17.392 --> 00:20.310
Oh, this is a Greenberg story.

00:20.311 --> 00:21.937
So, I got three voters against the wall.

00:21.938 --> 00:24.815
I caught 'em red-handed
disseminating pamphlets, right?

00:24.816 --> 00:27.067
- WLF stuff?
- I thought it was.

00:27.068 --> 00:28.819
Turned out later it was some,
like, religious crap,

00:28.820 --> 00:30.320
but I didn't fuckin' know that.

00:30.321 --> 00:33.575
So, I call for backup. Guess who shows up?

00:34.200 --> 00:36.618
- Greenberg!
- Greenberg!

00:36.619 --> 00:40.539
He pulls up, gets out of his truck.
He's in a fuckin' mood, okay?

00:40.540 --> 00:43.834
I can already tell, and he's all like,
"What are you fuckin' calling for?

00:43.835 --> 00:47.464
What, you can't handle three voters?
What did these fuckin' pussies even do?"

00:48.381 --> 00:51.884
I say, "I caught them
out here disseminating."

00:51.885 --> 00:55.679
And he goes, "What? You fuckin' perverts

00:55.680 --> 00:58.892
are out here jerking off
and splooging on my streets?"

00:59.851 --> 01:01.351
Holy shit!

01:01.352 --> 01:04.146
I swear to God.
So, one of the voters turns back

01:04.147 --> 01:06.273
to look at me like,
"Are you gonna tell him?"

01:06.274 --> 01:08.275
I look back at him like, "Fuck no."

01:08.276 --> 01:10.694
And that's when the guy decides
to open his mouth anyway

01:10.695 --> 01:14.908
and goes, "Well, actually, the word
'disseminate' means--" And...

01:16.159 --> 01:18.619
Greenberg slams his fuckin' head
against the wall.

01:18.620 --> 01:22.039
There goes his teeth,
just blood fuckin' everywhere.

01:22.040 --> 01:24.125
And Greenberg goes,

01:25.001 --> 01:27.921
"No one asked you, jizz boy!"

01:37.931 --> 01:40.058
Why do you call them that?

01:44.062 --> 01:46.106
The citizens, why do you call them voters?

01:47.107 --> 01:48.524
I don't know.

01:48.525 --> 01:50.692
'Cause that's what we fucking call 'em.
Who cares?

01:50.693 --> 01:52.695
'Cause we took away their rights.

01:56.741 --> 01:58.158
Took away their right to vote

01:58.159 --> 02:00.537
and somebody started calling them
voters to mock them.

02:03.998 --> 02:05.208
So, now you know.

02:10.505 --> 02:11.922
I didn't mean anything by it, Sergeant.

02:11.923 --> 02:13.842
Of course, you didn't.
You're thoughtless.

02:15.176 --> 02:16.469
Sarge.

02:32.861 --> 02:33.944
Keep it running.

02:33.945 --> 02:36.072
- Copy.
- How many?

02:36.906 --> 02:37.990
A lot.

02:37.991 --> 02:39.992
Could be WLF. Lock and load.

02:39.993 --> 02:41.953
- No.
- Sarge.

02:42.996 --> 02:45.622
I'm gonna go talk to them.
Alone.

02:45.623 --> 02:47.249
- But protocol.
- Protocol is to obey

02:47.250 --> 02:49.793
your commanding officer.
Period. The end.

02:49.794 --> 02:53.089
Now, if we go out there in force,
this'll end up the way it always does.

02:54.090 --> 02:55.633
'Cause you're all Greenberg.

03:00.430 --> 03:02.599
You wanna die? Fine.

03:19.115 --> 03:20.200
You.

03:22.702 --> 03:24.078
Come with me.

03:26.206 --> 03:27.290
Learn something.

03:57.570 --> 03:58.738
You Isaac?

04:02.408 --> 04:03.868
You Hanrahan?

04:54.711 --> 04:55.878
Welcome to the fight.

05:04.595 --> 05:06.264
Now, make your choice.

06:40.149 --> 06:41.359
No pain meds.

06:42.151 --> 06:43.653
Anything else?

06:44.320 --> 06:46.364
Probably nothing anyone wanted.

07:01.337 --> 07:03.088
You rockin' a yeast infection?

07:03.089 --> 07:05.883
Not today, but gimme time.

07:10.263 --> 07:12.849
Good news.
I found a gallon jug of milk.

07:14.225 --> 07:17.562
Make sure to smell it first, just in case.

07:19.021 --> 07:22.066
Alright, I give up.
I'm gonna stand watch outside.

07:22.775 --> 07:24.484
Yeah, I'm done.

07:24.485 --> 07:26.320
There's nothing else back h--

07:30.783 --> 07:32.118
Hey, I'm gonna pee.

07:32.994 --> 07:34.286
Gimme a minute.

07:34.287 --> 07:35.538
Okay.

08:02.315 --> 08:04.150
'Kay, good to go.

08:12.492 --> 08:13.576
Thanks.

08:15.119 --> 08:16.204
You okay?

08:17.497 --> 08:18.539
Yeah.

08:24.754 --> 08:27.006
Alright, hit it. People to kill.

08:28.466 --> 08:29.842
Okay.

08:41.020 --> 08:43.980
I don't understand.
I thought they bombed here.

08:43.981 --> 08:47.026
Yeah, I heard that too.
Guess not this part.

08:53.824 --> 08:55.492
What's up with all the rainbows?

08:55.493 --> 08:56.618
I don't know.

08:56.619 --> 08:59.038
Maybe they were all optimists.

09:13.636 --> 09:16.389
So much for happy, proud Rainbow Town.

09:22.228 --> 09:24.229
I've never seen a tank this close.

09:24.230 --> 09:25.898
Me neither.

09:27.608 --> 09:30.151
- Ellie. Ellie!
- Just cover me.

09:30.152 --> 09:32.238
I'm gonna check
if there's any ammo in there.

09:47.503 --> 09:50.047
Man, FEDRA got fucked up out here.

09:50.673 --> 09:52.382
You think it was the WLF?

09:52.383 --> 09:56.303
I don't know.
All these bodies are in FEDRA gear.

09:56.304 --> 09:58.222
Almost looks like
they were fighting each other.

09:59.390 --> 10:00.683
Good eye.

10:01.726 --> 10:03.144
I wonder what that was about.

10:23.289 --> 10:24.414
What is it?

10:24.415 --> 10:27.459
Three burnt skeletons.
Like Apollo 1.

10:27.460 --> 10:28.753
What?

10:29.420 --> 10:32.797
Grissom, White, Chaffee.
Early astronauts.

10:32.798 --> 10:35.008
They were supposed to be
the first ones to go to the moon

10:35.009 --> 10:37.093
but they never made it off the launchpad.

10:37.094 --> 10:38.596
Burned up in their capsule.

10:40.598 --> 10:44.684
Well, at least they died
for something worthwhile.

10:44.685 --> 10:46.186
Yeah.

10:46.187 --> 10:48.856
These guys were just assholes
killed by other assholes.

10:51.108 --> 10:52.818
Well, lookie here.

10:54.945 --> 10:56.489
Check out the building on the hill.

10:59.909 --> 11:01.619
You've gotta be shitting me.

11:04.747 --> 11:06.706
Fuck yeah, let's go.

11:06.707 --> 11:08.209
You sure about that?

11:14.882 --> 11:16.676
Oh, my God, are you gonna fucking tell me?

11:18.135 --> 11:20.679
If you paint a sign big enough
to be seen for miles away,

11:20.680 --> 11:22.514
that means you want people
to know that you're there,

11:22.515 --> 11:25.392
which also means more likely than not,
you're prepared.

11:25.393 --> 11:27.103
And?

11:29.063 --> 11:31.273
They're on a hill,
so they'll see us coming.

11:32.650 --> 11:36.362
On horseback in broad daylight,
so just a little.

11:37.363 --> 11:39.156
So, we wait until dark
and we head out on foot.

11:40.199 --> 11:41.950
And right here
is the perfect place to hole up

11:41.951 --> 11:43.952
because, well, no one's around.

11:43.953 --> 11:47.622
Which you proved brilliantly
with your tank hatch maneuver.

11:47.623 --> 11:48.833
Dick.

11:49.959 --> 11:52.502
Alright, let's look for a door
we can fit Shimmer through.

11:52.503 --> 11:54.088
Already found that.

13:13.083 --> 13:14.959
Shout if something tries to kill you!

13:14.960 --> 13:16.170
That's the plan.

15:21.629 --> 15:22.755
Go on.

15:23.589 --> 15:24.590
Okay.

17:14.283 --> 17:15.909
You've gotten pretty good.

17:19.329 --> 17:22.541
Thanks.
All those lessons from Joel.

17:24.334 --> 17:25.669
He taught you well.

17:27.963 --> 17:29.089
He did.

17:32.760 --> 17:34.844
- You hungry?
- Starving.

17:34.845 --> 17:37.639
Great. Come on.
I'll make us beef jerky.

17:40.059 --> 17:41.268
Okay.

18:16.095 --> 18:21.724
You know, when I was a younger man,
and I wanted to impress a woman,

18:21.725 --> 18:24.185
well, you have to know your strengths.

18:24.186 --> 18:26.772
And I was kinda shy.

18:27.397 --> 18:29.023
I didn't know how to talk to women.

18:29.024 --> 18:30.691
It made me nervous.

18:30.692 --> 18:34.696
So, what I would do is cook for them.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.866
And I was good.

18:39.076 --> 18:42.453
Good enough to deserve quality tools,
but did I have the money for that?

18:42.454 --> 18:43.789
No, I did not.

18:44.790 --> 18:49.837
I would go into Williams-Sonoma.
It's a cookware store. You wouldn't know.

18:52.131 --> 18:55.676
And I would stare

18:56.510 --> 18:57.761
at these.

18:59.179 --> 19:00.263
Mauviel.

19:00.264 --> 19:02.474
Best of the best. French, of course.

19:04.059 --> 19:05.768
And I would think, okay,

19:05.769 --> 19:08.980
30 years to retirement and pension,
but one day,

19:08.981 --> 19:12.151
I will own a Mauviel sauce pan

19:14.194 --> 19:15.736
with lid.

19:15.737 --> 19:17.156
And I was right.

19:19.825 --> 19:21.451
Just not how I planned.

19:26.707 --> 19:29.209
The strange benefits of the apocalypse.

19:35.841 --> 19:38.593
Now, copper's a bit of a pain in the ass.
You have to polish it a lot.

19:38.594 --> 19:41.095
But it heats faster than anything.

19:41.096 --> 19:42.639
Highly conductive.

19:43.724 --> 19:45.725
Of course,
this means it doesn't retain heat

19:45.726 --> 19:48.060
the way cast iron does, which of the two,

19:48.061 --> 19:51.106
makes copper the inferior choice
for interrogations, but

19:52.774 --> 19:56.486
if you own Mauviel, you use Mauviel.

19:58.989 --> 20:00.364
She--

20:00.365 --> 20:02.992
- She watches over me.
- Then she's been watching you

20:02.993 --> 20:04.369
get your ass kicked.

20:05.370 --> 20:07.371
You know there are even Scars
who don't believe

20:07.372 --> 20:09.290
she's some magic fairy in the sky, yeah?

20:09.291 --> 20:11.876
Some of you actually understand
she was just a person.

20:11.877 --> 20:13.545
Heretics.

20:15.297 --> 20:16.381
Of course.

20:19.009 --> 20:20.844
The steel handles stay cool.

20:21.511 --> 20:22.721
It's the little touches.

20:34.274 --> 20:36.693
Where are the Scars attacking next?

20:41.198 --> 20:42.616
Seraphites.

20:45.494 --> 20:46.995
Hold out your hand.

21:03.220 --> 21:05.429
Jesus. This is so fucked.

21:05.430 --> 21:08.100
Shut up. Isaac knows what he's doing.

21:12.980 --> 21:15.107
The blood!

21:16.233 --> 21:17.484
Yes, sir.

21:19.278 --> 21:27.743
She watches over me. She fills my soul.

21:27.744 --> 21:29.912
- She watches over--
- She fills your soul.

21:29.913 --> 21:31.998
You put an arrow in a little boy's head.

21:31.999 --> 21:34.375
Was she filling your soul then?

21:34.376 --> 21:36.085
She tell you to kill children?

21:36.086 --> 21:38.546
- You kill our children.
- Never by choice.

21:38.547 --> 21:40.214
You trained them to shoot at us.

21:40.215 --> 21:41.674
Because your Wolves kill them.

21:41.675 --> 21:43.718
Because you trained them to shoot at us.

21:43.719 --> 21:45.386
Because you broke the truce.

21:45.387 --> 21:46.929
- Because you broke the truce.
- Because--

21:46.930 --> 21:48.639
Because you broke it because we broke it.

21:48.640 --> 21:50.933
I'm not playing your
little chicken-and-egg games today, Scar.

21:50.934 --> 21:53.520
Where is the next attack?

22:01.570 --> 22:03.572
You're gonna lose.

22:05.449 --> 22:06.658
Are we?

22:08.869 --> 22:09.953
Son,

22:11.913 --> 22:14.248
we have automatic weapons and hospitals

22:14.249 --> 22:20.047
and you lunatics have bolt-action rifles,
bows and arrows, and superstition.

22:21.840 --> 22:24.801
So, tell me, how are we going to lose?

22:31.725 --> 22:36.812
Every day, one of your Wolves
comes to see the truth

22:36.813 --> 22:38.606
and takes Her into their heart.

22:38.607 --> 22:42.568
Every day.
Every day, a Wolf leaves you

22:42.569 --> 22:46.530
to take the holy mortification
to become a Seraphite.

22:46.531 --> 22:50.619
And none of us ever leave

22:51.703 --> 22:53.163
to become a Wolf.

22:57.042 --> 23:01.797
I will burn every part of you
until you tell me what I want to know!

23:18.438 --> 23:19.439
Good.

23:24.403 --> 23:26.279
Scar got what he deserved.

23:30.200 --> 23:31.618
Fucking animal.

23:36.456 --> 23:37.707
No patrol.

23:39.000 --> 23:41.211
- That's a good sign.
- Not always.

23:42.921 --> 23:45.423
So, the front entrance
is like a security door.

23:45.424 --> 23:47.383
There's a camera right over it,
which means we go

23:47.384 --> 23:48.885
around the back.

23:50.887 --> 23:52.013
Window.

23:54.808 --> 23:56.977
Oh, boy.

23:59.020 --> 24:00.397
Second floor.

24:06.903 --> 24:10.656
So, somebody hopped onto the shed,
climbed the downspout, broke the window,

24:10.657 --> 24:12.242
and got cut on the way in?

24:13.618 --> 24:15.620
Well, I guess that's our way in, too.

24:16.788 --> 24:19.749
And if we run into Wolves
that weren't in Jackson?

24:27.674 --> 24:28.717
Agreed.

24:42.564 --> 24:44.441
You can do that. You're good.

25:08.673 --> 25:11.426
What the fuck is this?

25:18.850 --> 25:21.102
- He isn't one of them.
- No.

25:23.605 --> 25:25.941
But we're definitely in the right place.

26:09.859 --> 26:10.860
Dina?

26:11.653 --> 26:12.779
Ellie, go.

26:20.745 --> 26:22.664
These aren't any of them either.

26:53.570 --> 26:56.323
That group we saw in the woods,
they did this.

26:57.240 --> 26:59.159
What the fuck is wrong with Seattle?

27:14.049 --> 27:15.508
It's the same ones we use.

27:16.217 --> 27:18.470
- If she called for backup--
- Yeah, we gotta get outta here.

27:19.346 --> 27:20.847
Shit, get down. Down!

27:26.686 --> 27:27.854
Oh, my God.

27:30.607 --> 27:31.816
Fuck me.

27:33.610 --> 27:35.653
- Look at this.
- Who the fuck would do that?

27:35.654 --> 27:37.696
Scars got all of 'em.

27:37.697 --> 27:41.618
I don't see Brancaccio or Welsh,
but, yeah, it's the rest of 'em.

27:42.994 --> 27:44.536
You, cut 'em down.

27:44.537 --> 27:46.163
Shouldn't we secure the station first?

27:46.164 --> 27:47.999
I said cut them the fuck down.

27:48.625 --> 27:51.126
The rest of you, fan out. And go slow.

27:51.127 --> 27:53.921
If the Scars are still here,
find them and kill them.

27:53.922 --> 27:55.714
Isaac said he wants 'em alive
for questioning.

27:55.715 --> 27:57.299
Isaac's not here, okay?

27:57.300 --> 27:59.009
With intestines
all over the fuckin' place.

27:59.010 --> 28:00.594
So, I don't really give a shit.

28:00.595 --> 28:02.971
I don't give a shit
if it's a woman or a kid.

28:02.972 --> 28:06.016
I don't care if it's a fuckin' baby.
Look what they did.

28:06.017 --> 28:07.811
Now, fan the fuck out!

28:15.402 --> 28:16.695
Clear!

28:25.870 --> 28:27.163
This side's clear.

28:32.585 --> 28:33.837
Clear.

28:44.139 --> 28:45.140
Clear!

28:57.902 --> 28:58.987
Clear.

29:02.198 --> 29:03.491
Stairs clear.

29:55.210 --> 29:56.294
We got one!

30:02.050 --> 30:03.176
Shoot that window!

30:04.594 --> 30:06.137
Move, move, move, move!

30:08.306 --> 30:09.557
Go!

30:12.936 --> 30:14.020
Come on!

30:22.904 --> 30:24.614
Come on. Get up!

30:41.089 --> 30:43.257
- Fuck!
- Shit!

30:43.258 --> 30:44.759
This way!

30:48.304 --> 30:50.306
- Aw, shit!
- Fuck!

30:52.225 --> 30:54.059
We see them! We see them!

30:54.060 --> 30:55.811
Go. We can fit, they can't.

30:55.812 --> 30:57.480
Come on, come on, come on, come on.

31:10.159 --> 31:13.246
They're in the transit tunnel.
Circle the south entrance.

32:00.084 --> 32:01.085
Okay.

32:02.503 --> 32:03.503
You good?

32:03.504 --> 32:04.756
Yeah.

32:07.216 --> 32:09.468
Is this place gonna fall down on us?

32:09.469 --> 32:10.970
I'd rather not find out.

32:11.429 --> 32:12.972
Let's go. That way.

33:19.455 --> 33:21.708
I thought it was supposed to be empty.

33:24.627 --> 33:25.920
Yeah. It was.

34:11.924 --> 34:12.925
This way!

34:15.303 --> 34:16.304
Dina!

34:21.184 --> 34:22.268
Ellie, fast!

34:29.859 --> 34:31.027
Shit!

34:35.073 --> 34:36.324
Go! Go!

34:41.913 --> 34:43.664
Oh, my God! Go, go, go!

35:18.616 --> 35:20.535
- Fuck!
- Get it!

35:26.332 --> 35:27.541
Ellie!

35:27.542 --> 35:28.751
Up!

35:32.380 --> 35:33.422
Shit!

35:36.509 --> 35:37.510
Ellie!

35:50.398 --> 35:51.399
Jump!

36:00.908 --> 36:02.160
The fence!

36:38.404 --> 36:40.198
Fucking open!

36:45.119 --> 36:46.162
Fucking move!

37:22.031 --> 37:23.407
Dina.

37:24.158 --> 37:25.201
Come on!

37:28.079 --> 37:29.205
Dina, come on!

37:39.090 --> 37:40.258
Maybe there.

37:44.512 --> 37:46.555
Come on, we've gotta get outta sight!

38:10.705 --> 38:13.332
We can hole up here for now.
I'll bar the door.

38:29.890 --> 38:31.975
Okay, it's not perfect,
but if anyone tries to get in,

38:31.976 --> 38:33.477
it'll buy us some ti...

38:37.148 --> 38:39.275
The fuck are you doing?

38:47.825 --> 38:48.826
Okay.

38:51.078 --> 38:54.080
Okay. Okay, I know you're scared.

38:54.081 --> 38:56.624
- Please, don't.
- But I need you to understand something.

38:56.625 --> 38:58.585
Please don't make this
any harder than it has to be.

38:58.586 --> 39:00.211
- Wait.
- Why did you do that?

39:00.212 --> 39:01.921
Why the fuck did you have to do that?

39:01.922 --> 39:03.381
Please listen to me.

39:03.382 --> 39:07.053
I would die for you. I would.
But that is not what just happened.

39:11.849 --> 39:13.392
Fuck. I'm immune.

39:14.143 --> 39:15.519
I can't get infected.

39:20.649 --> 39:22.443
Dina, do not fucking shoot me!

39:23.402 --> 39:25.905
I've been bitten before.
I'm still here.

39:27.990 --> 39:30.367
I don't-- I know you don't believe me.

39:30.368 --> 39:33.037
I get it,
I wouldn't believe me either, but...

39:35.331 --> 39:36.998
Here's what we're gonna do.

39:36.999 --> 39:39.751
I'm gonna walk over there nice and slow,

39:39.752 --> 39:41.544
to that big fucking chair,
and I'm gonna bandage my arm

39:41.545 --> 39:42.962
and I'm gonna go to sleep.

39:42.963 --> 39:45.215
You're gonna sit as far away from me
as you want

39:45.216 --> 39:47.258
and you're gonna keep
that gun pointed on me.

39:47.259 --> 39:50.388
If I turn, shoot me. But I promise.

39:51.889 --> 39:54.225
A lot of the times,
I wish this wasn't true,

39:57.561 --> 40:00.064
I'm gonna wake up
exactly as I am right now.

40:03.109 --> 40:04.360
Me.

40:10.533 --> 40:11.534
Okay.

40:48.195 --> 40:50.656
It's just water!
Rain fell on my face. That's all.

41:00.249 --> 41:03.294
See? No shaking.

41:06.922 --> 41:08.549
I'm gonna stand up now.

41:22.897 --> 41:24.482
Can I show you?

42:39.098 --> 42:40.683
Ellie.

42:41.642 --> 42:42.643
Yeah?

42:48.983 --> 42:50.401
I'm pregnant.

42:54.947 --> 42:56.240
What?

44:06.810 --> 44:07.935
Wait, no!

44:07.936 --> 44:10.105
No. Morning breath.

44:10.731 --> 44:12.941
It's gross. Hold on.

44:26.288 --> 44:28.289
I don't know if this is gonna be better.

44:28.290 --> 44:29.541
It'll be better.

44:38.676 --> 44:39.677
Beefy.

44:58.195 --> 44:59.488
How's it doing?

45:02.366 --> 45:03.534
That's...

45:11.792 --> 45:13.961
Is this where you were bitten before?

45:14.753 --> 45:15.754
Yep.

45:17.381 --> 45:20.300
- You said it was a burn.
- Most of it is.

45:24.179 --> 45:25.723
You did it to yourself?

45:28.559 --> 45:30.936
I really wanted to wear
short sleeves again.

45:35.441 --> 45:36.649
It's a little thing, but when you start

45:36.650 --> 45:38.484
to hide little things,
they become big things.

45:38.485 --> 45:39.862
You don't say.

45:49.580 --> 45:50.748
Why now?

45:59.131 --> 46:00.799
I thought you were gone.

46:04.094 --> 46:06.304
And then all of a sudden,

46:06.305 --> 46:08.098
this future I was imagining

46:10.184 --> 46:11.518
wasn't gonna happen.

46:14.438 --> 46:18.442
Where we're together,
and we have a kid, and...

46:20.611 --> 46:22.279
I don't even know if you want that.

46:25.282 --> 46:26.784
I want it with you.

46:31.246 --> 46:33.457
I'm sorry it took so long.

46:35.250 --> 46:36.752
I knew how you felt about me.

46:37.836 --> 46:40.922
How? I was hiding it really well.

46:40.923 --> 46:43.508
No, you kind of fucking weren't.

46:43.509 --> 46:45.384
I'm sorry.

46:45.385 --> 46:47.012
I wanted to.

46:47.638 --> 46:48.722
Yeah?

46:52.810 --> 46:54.353
When I was little,

46:56.480 --> 46:59.732
I told my mother I liked boys
and I liked girls.

46:59.733 --> 47:03.028
And she said, "No, you like boys."

47:05.239 --> 47:06.615
And it just...

47:09.576 --> 47:12.496
I got stuck.

47:14.414 --> 47:16.083
Even after she died, it...

47:18.877 --> 47:20.963
I tried to make things work with Jesse

47:21.922 --> 47:24.758
because I like him.
I do, I think he's a really good guy.

47:26.218 --> 47:28.512
But he wasn't the one.

47:31.682 --> 47:33.100
Still kept trying anyway.

47:34.893 --> 47:38.522
Couldn't let myself just be.

47:41.900 --> 47:43.777
You were scared.

47:45.904 --> 47:48.155
Not everyone's as brave as you.

47:48.156 --> 47:50.868
I'm not brave. I'm just obvious.

47:53.537 --> 47:54.955
Shut up!

48:17.978 --> 48:20.105
How do you know for sure that you're...

48:22.399 --> 48:23.900
I started wondering

48:23.901 --> 48:26.485
after we saw the bodies in the forest

48:26.486 --> 48:28.988
because I've seen fucked-up shit before
without barfing.

48:28.989 --> 48:31.991
And I knew morning sickness was a thing

48:31.992 --> 48:34.535
and I was late, which I--
I've never been regular,

48:34.536 --> 48:36.746
but I was very late.

48:36.747 --> 48:39.540
And then,
I found a pregnancy test

48:39.541 --> 48:42.627
at the pharmacy, and I peed on it.

48:42.628 --> 48:44.921
- You pee on it?
- That's how it works.

48:44.922 --> 48:46.589
I don't just randomly piss on stuff.

48:46.590 --> 48:48.215
Oh, okay. That's good.

48:48.216 --> 48:49.301
Here.

48:50.469 --> 48:51.887
Two lines means pregnant.

48:54.097 --> 48:55.723
This thing's pretty old.

48:55.724 --> 48:57.100
- How do you--
- And here.

48:58.477 --> 49:00.270
And here's a couple more.

49:08.987 --> 49:11.782
So, we're having a baby.

49:13.533 --> 49:16.161
I mean, we and also I guess Jesse are--

49:16.995 --> 49:18.413
It was Jesse, right?

49:21.792 --> 49:24.002
So, we're all having a baby.

49:25.796 --> 49:26.964
Holy shit.

49:30.717 --> 49:33.929
- I'm gonna be a dad.
- Yeah.

49:38.183 --> 49:40.184
...south of Pike. Heavy fire.

49:40.185 --> 49:41.978
Scars broke through
the north side of the FOB.

49:41.979 --> 49:44.021
- Casualties?
- At least two dozen.

49:44.022 --> 49:46.858
We're falling back.
Bringing wounded to Lakehill.

49:47.859 --> 49:49.694
Tell Nora to get ready.

49:49.695 --> 49:51.196
Oh, fuck!

49:55.492 --> 49:57.159
- He just said Nora.
- Yeah.

49:57.160 --> 49:59.286
- She's gonna know--
- Where Abby is, yeah.

49:59.287 --> 50:02.790
That's Lakehill but I don't know
where we are anymore.

50:02.791 --> 50:05.002
Okay, we go up high
and we look around. Come on.

50:34.072 --> 50:35.157
Ellie.

50:36.491 --> 50:38.743
See that white building out there?

50:38.744 --> 50:41.538
That's it. That's Lakehill.

50:55.135 --> 50:57.887
You don't have to go. You can stay here.

50:57.888 --> 50:59.681
- Fuck you.
- No, I'm not saying...

51:01.808 --> 51:04.143
- It's different now.
- Yes, it is.

51:04.144 --> 51:05.979
Will you please just think about it?

51:27.709 --> 51:28.919
Together.
